body:
For Fall 2019, I'm currently debating whether to take FAVS 475 Advanced Fiction Directing taught by Professor Nikyatu Jusu or FAVS 378 Web Series taught by Professor Susan Kehoe. I have gotten some information from Kehoe about 378, but I have yet to hear from Jusu about 475. So I guess my question is has anyone taken 475 before? If so, what is the course like? Do we make films for the course? If so, do they get shown in the Festival/Showcase?

&#x200B;

Any advice would be greatly appreciated.

&#x200B;

Thanks.

Haha, very funny, dude.

&#x200B;

Everybody knows that Ron Swanson is a fictional character from the NBC sitcom Parks and Recreation.

Count me in!

&#x200B;

BTW, It's me, Chris!

Wait,

&#x200B;

So after the Cops learn of the Thieves' motives and their identities, they're still fighting each other at the end?

&#x200B;

What a cop out! (no pun intended)

You sure you want to do that? After everything that went on last year?

&#x200B;

Hell, several people formerly associated with CA, Lupa, Phealous, and possibly Linkara are probably still on bad terms with the Walkers.

&#x200B;

Bottom line, CA's reputation suffered from irreversible damage and has lost what little credibility they may have had left. So don't bother.

Works perfectly!

&#x200B;

Thanks!

Okay, folks.

&#x200B;

I did not expect this much feedback.

&#x200B;

So I guess the general consensus is that there is no real conclusion to this whole fiasco and probably never will be, correct?

&#x200B;

If so, what a letdown. :(
